## The library pin

Every `include:` in `.gitlab-ci.yml` pins a release tag of `{{ lib_project }}`,
and moving those pins changes what gates this repo. The tag lives in **one** place —
`variables.WEISSSRV_LIB_REF`. GitLab forbids a variable in `include: ref:`, so
`scripts/check-lib-pins.py --fix` syncs those literals and the `lib-pin-check`
job fails the pipeline on any that drift or pin a branch. A bump is one edit plus
`--fix`, and re-vendoring the library copies under `scripts/` from the new tag in
the same {{ change_request }}: `check-doc-links.py`, `check-lib-pins.py`,
`check-netpol-except-parity.py` and `semantic-release.py`. No gate here notices an
edit to a vendored file; a re-vendor overwrites it. `check-kustomization.py` and
`check-scrape-wiring.py` are this repo's own, so edit those here.
{%- elif ci_shape == 'github' %}

## Vendored workflows

`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `release.yml` and `build-image.yml` are vendored
from the shared library rather than referenced, because GitHub has no equivalent
of GitLab's `include: project:` for a private library. Tool versions and their
sha256 pins are literals there. Re-vendor those three files and the library
copies `scripts/check-doc-links.py`, `scripts/check-netpol-except-parity.py` and
`scripts/semantic-release.py` from the library tag you move to, in one
{{ change_request }}. They come from the shared **weisssrv-lib** project, and
this repo records no library ref, so name the tag you vendored in the
{{ change_request }}. `.github/workflows/manifest-gates.yml`,
`scripts/check-kustomization.py` and `scripts/check-scrape-wiring.py` are this
repo's own, not library copies.

One hand edit is expected: `env.K8S_VERSION` in `ci.yml` carries the library's
own literal, which a byte-identical copy cannot take from an answer. Set it to
this cluster's Kubernetes minor, `{{ k8s_version }}`, the value `Taskfile.yml`
uses. Re-apply it in the same pull request as every re-vendor: the copy
overwrites it, and no gate in this repo notices.
{%- else %}

## The vendored files

`scripts/check-doc-links.py` and `scripts/check-netpol-except-parity.py` are
byte-identical copies of library files. This repo carries no gate that notices an
edit to one, and a re-vendor overwrites it. Change them upstream, or re-vendor
both from a single library tag and say so in the {{ change_request }}.
`scripts/check-kustomization.py` and `scripts/check-scrape-wiring.py` are this
repo's own: change them here.
{%- endif %}

## Updating from the template

This repo was generated by copier and records its answers in
`.copier-answers.yml`. `copier update` replays them against a newer template
tag, so a template fix reaches this repo as a reviewable diff. Flipping an
answer (say `enable_hpa`) is the same operation — pass `--data enable_hpa=true`
or answer the prompt again.
